      "message": "feat(ui): the Report door shoots the whole window\n\nThe maintainer's GUI test on PR #1798 said the picture must be the\nwhole application window, not just the 3D model area.\n\nThe door asks the shell for a window picture the way egui intends: it\npushes ViewportCommand::Screenshot with a private token; the frame loop\nre-renders this frame's shapes into a private texture in a second\nrender pass, reads it back, and answers egui with an\nEvent::Screenshot. The door copies the answer to the clipboard when the\ntoken matches. egui_wgpu's capture feature was dropped unread: its\nread-back rejects our Bgra8UnormSrgb surface. SolidCraft was read as\nmechanism reference only - no code, no look (their brand licence).\n\nThe CPU-raster path (the ground-grid fix of 26e17a81) is superseded;\nits helpers (raster::ground_line, Camera::scale, the interact\nvisibility widenings) had no other user and are reverted.\n\nLedger: docs/decisions/1696-report-button.md.\nPinned by: the 15 report_tests, including\nthe_shot_token_matches_only_itself.",
